-- MANUAL REVIEW: Q530 — Label changed from B to D — verify explanation reasoning matches choice D
-- Q530: Fix #6
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 453, the installment method recognizes gain proportionally as payments are received. Mitchell's 60% gross profit percentage means each $100,000 payment includes $60,000 of gain and $40,000 of basis recovery. Over five years, Mitchell recognizes $60,000 per year, totaling $300,000 — the same total gain as O'Brien, but spread over time. O'Brien receives all cash at closing and recognizes the full $300,000 immediately. The economic rationale is that taxpayers should not be required to pay tax on gain before receiving the cash to pay it. Without the installment method, Mitchell would owe tax on $300,000 in year one despite receiving only $100,000. (A) is wrong because gain is not deferred to the final year — it is recognized proportionally with each payment. (C) is wrong because the installment method remains available for most non-dealer sales. (D) reverses the application — the installment method applies to deferred-payment sales, not lump-sum sales.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 530;

