  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): The installment method under Section 453 calculates a gross profit percentage (total gain / contract price) that applies to each payment received. Harper: ($200,000 − $120,000) / $200,000 = 40%. Mercer: ($200,000 − $160,000) / $200,000 = 20%. When Harper receives the $50,000 down payment, 40% ($20,000) is gain and 60% ($30,000) is return of basis. Mercer recognizes only $10,000 gain on the same down payment. The lower basis produces a higher percentage, meaning more of each dollar received is taxable. The installment method's key advantage is liquidity matching — sellers are not forced to pay tax on gain before receiving the cash, which is especially valuable when the seller finances the purchase over multiple years. (B) is wrong because the percentage depends on gain relative to price, which varies with basis. (C) confuses the formula — it uses basis/price instead of gain/price. (D) is wrong because the installment method applies regardless of whether a down payment is received; it is the default method for qualifying sales.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 531;

