-- MANUAL REVIEW: Q545 — Label changed from D to B — verify explanation reasoning matches choice B
-- Q545: Fix #6
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 469, passive losses can only offset passive income in the current year. Morrison's $30,000 of passive income from Activity A absorbs $30,000 of the $50,000 passive losses, leaving $20,000 suspended — wages cannot absorb the excess. However, the disposition rule is the critical analytical distinction: upon a fully taxable disposition of a passive activity, all suspended losses from that activity are released and become deductible against any income, including wages. This ensures that true economic losses are eventually recognized. (A) is wrong because passive losses cannot offset nonpassive income (wages, portfolio income) in the current year. (B) is wrong because having passive income is beneficial — it provides a source to absorb passive losses. (C) is wrong because the $25,000 rental allowance applies only to active participation in rental real estate, not general passive activities.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 545;

