  stem = $EXPL$In a transfer, a shareholder contributes property (basis $100,000, FMV $160,000) and a liability of $120,000 is assumed by the corporation. What is the shareholder's recognized gain?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$When liabilities assumed exceed the transferor's basis in the contributed property, the excess is recognized as gain under Section 357(c). Gain = liability assumed ($120,000) - basis ($100,000) = $20,000. The shareholder's stock basis becomes $0. (See Section 351.)$EXPL$
