-- MANUAL REVIEW: Q1178 — Label changed from A to D — verify explanation reasoning matches choice D
-- Q1178: Fix #6
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): The automatic stay under Section 362 is one of bankruptcy's most powerful protections, taking effect immediately upon filing. It halts virtually all civil collection actions: foreclosures, lawsuits, garnishments, repossessions, and collection communications. However, Section 362(b) contains specific exceptions, including criminal proceedings against the debtor — the IRS criminal investigation continues unaffected because allowing debtors to block criminal enforcement through bankruptcy would undermine the justice system. The consequence for stay violations is significant: under Section 362(k), an individual debtor injured by a willful violation may recover actual damages (including attorneys' fees) and, in appropriate cases, punitive damages. This enforcement mechanism gives the stay real teeth. (B) is wrong because the automatic stay explicitly exempts criminal proceedings and several other categories. (C) is wrong because the stay applies to both secured and unsecured creditors — all civil collection activity is halted. (D) is wrong because the stay takes effect immediately upon filing, not after a waiting period.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1178;

-- Q1187: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Brighton County presents both governmental fund financial statements and government-wide financial statements in its comprehensive annual financial report. requires a reconciliation between these two sets of statements. What is the primary reason this reconciliation is required?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct: Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 77, a reconciliation between governmental fund financial statements and government-wide financial statements is required because the two use fundamentally different measurement bases. Governmental funds use the current financial resources measurement focus and modified accrual basis, recognizing revenues when measurable and available, while government-wide statements use the economic resources measurement focus and full accrual basis, recognizing revenues when earned. This difference creates systematic reporting gaps for long-term assets, long-term liabilities, and accrual-based revenues that must be bridged through reconciliation, whereas fund statements alone would not capture the full economic position of the government. (See GASB 34.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1187;

