-- Q2603: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$In a exchange, both parties transfer mortgages. The taxpayer is relieved of a $150,000 mortgage and assumes a $90,000 mortgage on the replacement property. What is the net boot received?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under IRC Sec. 1031(b), gain is recognized in a like-kind exchange only to the extent of boot received. When both parties transfer mortgaged properties, the mortgages are netted per Treasury Reg. Sec. 1.1031(b)-1(c): mortgage relief of $150,000 minus the $90,000 mortgage assumed equals $60,000 in net boot received. This net amount determines the gain recognized. Unlike cash boot, which is straightforward, mortgage boot requires netting because assumption of a mortgage by the taxpayer offsets the boot effect of being relieved of a mortgage. (See Section 1031.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2603;

