-- Q3060: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$A valuation specialist is measuring the fair value of a corporate bond that trades infrequently. The specialist applies the market approach A Level 2 input in this measurement would be:$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 820-10-35-47 through 35-55, Level 2 inputs include quoted prices for similar assets in active markets, quoted prices for identical assets in inactive markets, and other observable market data such as interest rates, yield curves, and credit spreads. For an infrequently traded corporate bond, observable yield data from similar bonds qualifies as Level 2. In contrast, a quoted price for the exact same security in an active market is Level 1, whereas unobservable management assumptions constitute Level 3 inputs. (See ASC 820..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3060;

