-- Q4151: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$A corporation makes a $150,000 interest-free demand loan to its sole shareholder. The AFR is 4%., the forgone interest is treated as:$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$The correct answer is a constructive dividend to the shareholder and deemed interest income to the corporation. Under IRC Sec. 7872(a), below-market loans between a corporation and shareholder are recharacterized: forgone interest ($150,000 × 4% = $6,000) is treated as a deemed transfer from the corporation to the shareholder (constructive dividend) and a deemed interest payment back from the shareholder to the corporation. Unlike arm's-length loans where actual interest is paid, Sec. 7872 imputes both the dividend and the interest to prevent avoidance of the dividend and interest income rules. (See Section 7872.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4151;

