-- Q4342: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$The Westfield Community Foundation, a 3) organization, borrows $800,000 to purchase a commercial rental property expected to generate unrelated business income. The interest expense on this debt-financed property is:$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under IRC Sections 512 through 514, when a tax-exempt organization acquires debt-financed property, the income attributable to that property constitutes unrelated business taxable income (UBTI). Section 514(a) defines debt-financed property as any income-producing property with acquisition indebtedness. The interest expense on the borrowed funds is deductible only against the UBTI generated by that debt-financed property under Section 512(a)(1), not against the organization''s exempt function income. Unlike income from activities substantially related to the organization''s exempt purpose, debt-financed rental income is subject to UBIT regardless of how the proceeds are used. (See Section 501.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4342;

