-- Q4859: Fix #4, #9
UPDATE questions SET
  cognitive_level = 2,
  stem = $EXPL$Hartfield Inc. consolidates a wholly owned subsidiary in Japan whose functional currency is the yen. Hartfield applies the current rate method Which of the following balance sheet items is translated at historical exchange rates?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 830-10-45-17 (the current rate method), all assets and liabilities are translated at the current exchange rate as of the balance sheet date, while equity accounts such as common stock and additional paid-in capital are translated at historical rates in effect when the equity transactions originally occurred. Retained earnings is a composite amount built up from translated income statement items over time. Although translating all balance sheet items at the current rate might seem simpler, equity accounts retain historical rates because they represent capital transactions completed at specific past exchange rates. (See ASC 830..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4859;

