  stem = $EXPL$Fletcher dies on January 5, 2026, owning shares of Waverly Corp. valued at $400,000 at death. The executor elects the alternate valuation date . On July 5, 2026, the shares are worth $340,000 and have not been distributed. What is the beneficiary's income tax basis in the Waverly Corp. shares?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under IRC Sections 2032 and 1014(a), when the executor elects alternate valuation, the beneficiary's basis equals the fair market value on the alternate valuation date (six months after death) rather than the date-of-death value. The shares are valued at $340,000 on July 5, 2026. Choice A is incorrect because the alternate valuation election overrides the standard date-of-death valuation, and basis follows the value used for estate tax purposes. (See Section 2032.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 5179;

