-- Q5356: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$The County of Eastwood maintains a road network with a net book value of $53,000,000 ($85,000,000 cost less $32,000,000 accumulated depreciation). Annual depreciation is $3,400,000. The county spends approximately $2,800,000 annually on road preservation to maintain its condition target. The county considers switching to the modified approach What is the most likely effect on reported expenses in the government-wide financial statements?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under GASB 34, paragraphs 23-25, the modified approach replaces depreciation with expense recognition of preservation costs needed to maintain the established condition level. Since annual preservation costs ($2,800,000) are less than depreciation ($3,400,000), the switch reduces reported expenses by approximately $600,000. Choice B is incorrect because the modified approach eliminates depreciation — preservation costs replace rather than supplement depreciation expense. (See GASB 34..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 5356;

