-- Q5365: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$The City of Pine Valley reports the following pension-related items : net pension liability of $14,200,000, deferred outflows of resources related to pensions of $3,800,000, and deferred inflows of resources related to pensions of $2,100,000. The finance director asks how the deferred items affect the city's total net position compared to reporting only the net pension liability. What is the net effect of the deferred items on net position?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under GASB 63, deferred outflows of resources increase net position while deferred inflows of resources decrease net position. Net position equals assets plus deferred outflows minus liabilities minus deferred inflows. Compared to recognizing only the net pension liability, the deferred outflows ($3,800,000) increase net position and the deferred inflows ($2,100,000) decrease it, for a net improvement of $1,700,000. Choice A is incorrect because while deferred outflows will eventually become expenses, they currently function as asset-like items that increase net position. (See GASB 68.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 5365;

