-- Q5477: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$On October 1, 2026, Montgomery transfers $2,000,000 to a charitable remainder annuity trust that pays Montgomery $120,000 annually for 15 years, after which the remainder passes to a qualified charity. The present value of the charitable remainder interest is $820,000 under the tables. What is Montgomery's gift tax charitable deduction?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under IRC Section 2522(c)(2), a gift tax charitable deduction is allowed for the present value of the remainder interest passing to a qualifying charity from a charitable remainder annuity trust. The deduction equals $820,000, the actuarially determined value of the charity's remainder interest. Choice D is incorrect because retaining an income interest does not disqualify the charitable deduction; the Code specifically provides for split-interest trust deductions when the trust meets CRAT requirements. (See Section 7520.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 5477;

