-- Q8365: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Redfield Corp. has 250,000 weighted-average common shares and revenues of $5,000,000 with total expenses of $3,800,000, including $200,000 of share-based compensation expense Net income is $1,200,000. How does the stock compensation expense affect basic EPS?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 260-10-45-10, basic EPS uses reported net income as the numerator. Stock compensation expense under ASC 718 reduces net income like any other expense, directly lowering the basic EPS numerator. Basic EPS = $1,200,000 / 250,000 = $4.80. Choice A is incorrect because although stock compensation is noncash, it is recognized in the income statement and reduces net income, which is the numerator for basic EPS. (See ASC 718..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 8365;

