-- Q8431: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Harrington Corp. reports net income of $1,200,000 with 300,000 weighted-average common shares. On July 1, the company issued $500,000 of 8% convertible bonds, each $1,000 bond convertible into 20 shares. The tax rate is 25%. The CFO must determine whether to include these bonds in diluted EPS and how to weight them. Evaluate the correct treatment$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 260-10-45-40, convertible securities issued during the period are weighted from the issue date. The bonds were outstanding 6 months, so 500 bonds x 20 shares x 6/12 = 5,000 incremental shares. The after-tax interest add-back is $500,000 x 8% x 6/12 x (1 - 0.25) = $15,000. However, Choice D incorrectly uses $20,000 pre-tax instead of the after-tax amount, omitting the required tax adjustment. (See ASC 260..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 8431;

