-- Q10717: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Weber transfers property with a basis of $120,000 and FMV of $300,000, subject to a $90,000 mortgage, to a newly formed corporation for 100% of the stock in a exchange. The mortgage does not exceed the property's basis. What is Weber's basis in the stock received?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under Sections 358(a) and 358(d), the shareholder's stock basis equals the adjusted basis of property transferred ($120,000) decreased by the liability assumed ($90,000). Since the liability does not exceed basis, no gain is recognized under Section 357(c), and stock basis is $120,000 − $90,000 = $30,000. Choice A is incorrect because it ignores the liability reduction; Section 358(d) treats the assumption as money received for basis computation purposes. (See Section 351.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10717;

