-- Q10733: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Torres contributes a machine held for four years (basis $60,000, FMV $120,000) to a newly formed corporation for 100% of the stock . Six months after the exchange, the corporation sells the machine. What is the corporation's holding period for the machine?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under Section 1223(2), when a corporation acquires property with a transferred basis under Section 362, it tacks the transferor's holding period. The corporation includes Torres's four-year holding period plus its own six months, totaling four years and six months for capital gain characterization. Choice A is incorrect because it ignores the tacking rule; Section 1223(2) applies whenever the corporation's basis is determined by reference to the transferor's basis. (See Section 351.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10733;

