-- Q10809: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Branford Corp, a C corporation, sells a commercial building for $900,000. The building was purchased for $750,000, and accumulated straight-line depreciation is $200,000 (adjusted basis $550,000). No recapture exists because only straight-line depreciation was used. What additional recapture does Branford recognize ?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under IRC Section 291(a)(1), C corporations must recognize additional ordinary income equal to 20% of the amount that would have been recaptured under Section 1245 had the property been Section 1245 property. The additional recapture is 20% x $200,000 (total depreciation) = $40,000. Choice D is incorrect because Section 291 applies specifically to corporations regardless of depreciation method, requiring 20% of straight-line depreciation as ordinary income on real property. (See Section 1250.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 10809;

