-- Q11100: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Ridgemont Partners LP has a election in effect. Partner Shaw purchases a 25% interest for $400,000. The partnership's assets include cash of $200,000, accounts receivable of $200,000 (basis $0), equipment of $400,000 (basis $300,000, property), and goodwill of $800,000 (basis $100,000). Shaw's 25% share of inside basis is $150,000., evaluate how the $250,000 adjustment is allocated between the ordinary income and capital gain asset classes.$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under Section 755, the 743(b) adjustment is allocated between ordinary income assets (receivables, equipment) and capital gain assets (goodwill) based on the difference between the transferee's share of FMV and share of inside basis within each class. Shaw's share of ordinary FMV is $150,000 ($600,000 x 25%) vs. inside basis of $75,000, producing a $75,000 ordinary adjustment. Shaw's share of capital FMV is $200,000 vs. inside basis of $25,000, producing a $175,000 capital adjustment. The total $250,000 is not split equally (Choice B) because Section 755 requires FMV-based allocation to each class. (See Section 754.). (See Section 1245.). (See Section 743.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11100;

