-- Q11404: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$The City of Ridgecrest operates an internal service fund for fleet management that serves both city departments (80% of billings) and three neighboring towns under intergovernmental agreements (20% of billings). The fund's external billings have grown from 5% to 20% over three years. The city auditor questions whether the fund should be reclassified as an enterprise fund. Evaluate the most appropriate classification$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under GASB 34 (par. 67-68), an enterprise fund is required when fees are charged to external users as the primary revenue source or when legally required. An internal service fund predominantly serves internal departments. Since 80% of Ridgecrest's fleet billings remain internal, the fund's predominant purpose is still internal service delivery. Choice B is incorrect because GASB 34 does not mandate enterprise fund classification merely because some external billing exists. However, the city should disclose the external component and monitor whether the balance shifts. (See GASB 34..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11404;

