-- Q11586: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Kessler Enterprises disposes of a major product line that qualifies as a component of the entity The segment had an operating loss of $200,000 and a disposal gain of $50,000, both net of tax. Where are these amounts reported on the income statement?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 205-20-45-3, results of discontinued operations are reported net of tax as a separate component below income from continuing operations. Both the operating loss and disposal gain are presented within the discontinued operations section, not commingled with continuing operations. Option A is incorrect because discontinued operations must be segregated from operating expenses to enable users to assess ongoing earnings quality. (See ASC 205-20..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11586;

-- Q11596: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$, Hartwell Corp. elects the fair value option for a long-term liability. The liability's fair value decreases by $200,000 in 2025 — $60,000 from changes in its own credit risk and $140,000 from benchmark interest rate changes. Will the credit risk component ever be reclassified from OCI to net income under the PUFER framework?$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11596;

-- Q11610: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Blakemore Industries factors $400,000 of accounts receivable to Summit Finance on September 1, 2026, retaining an obligation to reimburse Summit for any uncollectible amounts. Summit advances 90% of the face value. The controller classifies the $360,000 advance as an operating cash inflow. Evaluate whether this classification is appropriate and$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 860-10-40, a transfer of receivables with recourse typically fails the sale criteria because the transferor retains effective control through the credit-loss obligation. When the transfer does not qualify as a sale, the advance is a secured borrowing classified as a financing activity under ASC 230-10-45-14. Choice A is incorrect because the recourse provision, not the underlying asset type, determines whether the cash flow is operating or financing. (See ASC 860..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11610;

-- Q11611: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Novak Industries holds a 60-day U.S. Treasury bill and a 9-month certificate of deposit. The controller is determining which instruments qualify as cash equivalents on the statement of cash flows., which characteristic defines a cash equivalent?$EXPL$
