-- Q11613: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Ferndale Corp. repurchases $1,000,000 face value bonds on the open market for $935,000 on June 15, 2026. The bonds have a carrying amount of $980,000 after unamortized premium. The CFO presents the $935,000 payment as a financing outflow and the $45,000 gain within operating activities under the indirect method. Evaluate whether the presentation of both items is correct$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 230-10-45-16, the $935,000 cash paid to retire debt is a financing outflow. The $45,000 gain ($980,000 carrying amount minus $935,000) is included in net income but relates to a financing transaction. Under the indirect method, the gain must be subtracted from net income in operating activities to prevent double-counting, since the full $935,000 already appears in financing. Choice A is incorrect because leaving the gain unadjusted in operating activities overstates operating cash flows. (See ASC 230..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11613;

