-- Q11623: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Pinnacle Financial holds a portfolio of short-term commercial paper with original maturities of 60 days. During Year 2, Pinnacle purchases $5,200,000 and receives $5,100,000 in maturities. The CFO proposes reporting only the net $100,000 investing outflow rather than gross purchases and maturities. Evaluate whether net reporting is permitted$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 230-10-45-9, certain investing and financing activities involving items that are quick turnover, large in amount, and short in maturity may be reported net. Commercial paper with 60-day maturities qualifies because the original maturity is under three months and turnover is rapid. This exception recognizes that gross reporting of high-volume, short-maturity items can obscure rather than illuminate cash flow patterns. Choice B is incorrect because ASC 230 provides a specific net reporting exception for qualifying short-maturity items. (See ASC 230..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11623;

-- Q11628: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Prescott Industries sells a warehouse with a book value of $500,000 to an unrelated buyer for $650,000 and simultaneously leases it back under an operating lease on July 1, 2026., the transaction qualifies as a sale. The $150,000 gain is recognized in net income. What is the most likely effect on the statement of cash flows under the indirect method?$EXPL$
