-- Q11632: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Mercer Holdings discontinues its retail division on October 1, 2026. During the wind-down, the division generates $85,000 in operating receipts, sells fixtures for $120,000, and repays a $200,000 division-specific loan. The CFO proposes combining all three items into a single line labeled 'Cash flows from discontinued operations' at the bottom of the statement. Evaluate whether this presentation complies with$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 230-10-50-4B, cash flows from discontinued operations must be presented within or disclosed by operating, investing, and financing categories. The $85,000 belongs in operating, the $120,000 in investing, and the $200,000 in financing activities. Combining them into one line obscures the nature of the cash flows and violates ASC 230's three-category framework. Choice A is incorrect because a single aggregated line does not satisfy the by-category presentation requirement. (See ASC 230..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11632;

