-- Q11666: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$During its 2025 annual review, Whitfield Industries discovered that a prior-year journal entry had been recorded incorrectly. The controller is researching the proper terminology The term ''restatement'' is specifically reserved for which type of accounting event?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$ASC 250-10-20 defines restatement as the process of revising previously issued financial statements to correct an error. The term "retrospective application" is used for changes in accounting principle, while "prospective application" describes estimate changes. Option A is incorrect because principle changes use retrospective application, not restatement. This terminology distinction is important for proper classification and disclosure. (See ASC 250..)$EXPL$
