-- Q11734: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$On January 1, 2026, First National Bank issues a $10 million note payable and elects the fair value option Issuance costs total $150,000. At December 31, 2026, the note's fair value is $9,800,000. How should First National account for the issuance costs and the year-end fair value change?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$ASC 825-10-25-3 requires that when the fair value option is elected, upfront costs and fees are recognized in earnings immediately — not deferred or capitalized. The decrease from $10,000,000 to $9,800,000 reduces the liability by $200,000, recognized as a gain in net income. Deferring issuance costs is incorrect because the fair value option eliminates the ability to capitalize transaction costs. (See ASC 825..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11734;

