-- Q11737: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Dalton Industries determines its reporting unit's carrying amount exceeds fair value by $2.4 million during goodwill impairment testing The goodwill balance is $5 million., how is this fair value measurement classified?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$ASC 820-10-50-1 classifies goodwill impairment as nonrecurring because goodwill is not remeasured at fair value every period — fair value is determined only when impairment testing is triggered. The annual test is a test for impairment, not a periodic remeasurement to fair value; goodwill remains at carrying amount unless impaired. (See ASC 350..)$EXPL$
