-- Q11755: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Oakmont Ventures holds an equity investment in a private company with no readily determinable fair value and elects the measurement alternative During the year, an observable transaction in the investee's stock occurs at a price indicating the investment is worth $150,000 more than Oakmont's carrying amount. How should Oakmont account for this?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$ASC 321-10-35-2 provides a measurement alternative: cost minus impairment, adjusted for observable price changes from orderly transactions in the same or similar securities. The $150,000 upward adjustment is recognized in net income, not OCI. OCI treatment applies to available-for-sale debt securities under ASC 326, not equity securities under the measurement alternative. (See ASC 321-10-35-2..)$EXPL$
