  stem = $EXPL$Cascade Corp. classifies a manufacturing plant as held for sale and writes it down from a carrying amount of $6.2 million to fair value less costs to sell of $5.5 million., this fair value measurement is classified as:$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$ASC 820-10-50-1 classifies fair value measurements of assets held for sale as nonrecurring. These assets are measured at the lower of carrying amount or fair value less costs to sell, so fair value is relevant only when a write-down occurs — it is not a periodic remeasurement to fair value as defined by ASC 820. Ongoing monitoring does not constitute a recurring fair value measurement. (See ASC 360-10-45.)$EXPL$
