  stem = $EXPL$Ashford City is preparing its government-wide statement of activities for the first time The finance director must organize reported activities into the required categories. Activities are separated into which two categories?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under GASB 34, paragraph 12, government-wide financial statements separate all activities into governmental activities (supported by taxes and grants) and business-type activities (financed by fees charged to external users). Fiduciary activities are excluded entirely. Choice D is incorrect because fiduciary activities are not reported in the government-wide statements, and the general fund is a fund-level concept, not a government-wide classification. (See GASB 34..)$EXPL$
