-- Q11768: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Maplewood School District provides retiree health insurance but has not established a trust to fund the obligation. The actuary calculates a total OPEB liability of $14.3 million. The finance director asks how the unfunded plan appears on the government-wide Statement of Net Position. Analyze the reporting effect$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under GASB 75, the net OPEB liability equals the total OPEB liability minus plan fiduciary net position. Because Maplewood has no trust (unfunded plan), plan assets are zero, so the full $14.3 million total OPEB liability is reported as the net OPEB liability on the government-wide Statement of Net Position. Choice B is incorrect because GASB 75 requires recognition of the liability regardless of funding status — note disclosure alone is insufficient. (See GASB 75..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11768;

