-- Q11795: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Foster Bank records a $2,400,000 allowance for credit losses (CECL) at year-end. For tax purposes, bad debts are deductible only when specifically charged off. During the year, $600,000 of loans were written off. The enacted tax rate is 21%. What deferred tax asset should Foster record related to the remaining allowance?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 740-10-25-20, the $2,400,000 credit loss allowance is a future deductible temporary difference because it is expensed for book purposes but not deductible for tax until loans are charged off. The DTA is $2,400,000 × 21% = $504,000. Option B incorrectly subtracts the $600,000 already written off, but those amounts have been deducted for both book and tax and are no longer part of the temporary difference. (See ASC 326.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11795;

-- Q11798: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Newkirk Labs spent $500,000 on research and development in Year 1. Under GAAP, the full amount is expensed immediately. For federal tax purposes, the costs must be capitalized and amortized over 5 years ($100,000 per year). The tax rate is 21%. What deferred tax effect should Newkirk record in Year 1?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 740-10-25-20, when GAAP expense ($500,000) exceeds the tax deduction ($100,000 amortization), taxable income exceeds book income by $400,000, creating a future deductible temporary difference. The DTA is $400,000 × 21% = $84,000. Option A incorrectly classifies this as a DTL; because more tax deductions will occur in future years, the difference creates future tax savings, not future obligations. (See Section 174.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11798;

-- Q11802: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$At December 31, 2025, Harmon Industries recorded a $350,000 increase in its deferred tax asset related to warranty obligations that are not yet deductible for tax purposes., what is a deferred tax benefit?$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11802;

