-- Q11812: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Saunders Corp. enters into a 5-year operating lease and recognizes a right-of-use asset of $450,000 and a lease liability of $450,000 at inception For tax purposes, no asset or liability is recognized; only the annual lease payments are deductible. The enacted tax rate is 21%. What is the net deferred tax effect at inception?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 740-10-25-20, the ROU asset (book $450,000, tax basis $0) creates a DTL of $94,500, while the lease liability (book $450,000, tax basis $0) creates an offsetting DTA of $94,500. At inception these net to zero. As the lease progresses, the asset and liability may amortize at different rates, creating a temporary net difference. Option A considers only the ROU asset without the offsetting DTA from the liability. (See ASC 842..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11812;

-- Q11814: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Underwood Mining records an asset retirement obligation of $500,000 in Year 1 By Year 3, the ARO liability has accreted to $560,000 and the capitalized asset retirement cost has been depreciated to a net book amount of $350,000. For tax purposes, no deduction occurs until retirement. The tax rate is 21%. What is the net deferred tax asset related to the ARO at Year 3?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 740-10-25-20, the ARO creates two temporary differences: the $560,000 liability (future deductible) and the $350,000 remaining capitalized cost (future taxable since tax basis is zero). The net deductible temporary difference is $560,000 − $350,000 = $210,000, yielding a DTA of $210,000 × 21% = $44,100. Option C considers only the liability without offsetting the asset's temporary difference. (See ASC 410..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11814;

