-- Q11833: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$A newly hired accountant at Cedar Valley Health Services, a not-for-profit hospital, is preparing year-end financial statements. The accountant asks what the not-for-profit equivalent of the for-profit balance sheet is called$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 958-210, an NFP entity reports its assets, liabilities, and net assets on the statement of financial position. This serves the same purpose as the for-profit balance sheet but uses NFP-specific terminology reflecting the absence of owners' equity. Unlike the "statement of net position," which is a governmental accounting term under GASB, the statement of financial position is the correct term for private NFPs under FASB standards. (See ASC 958..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11833;

