-- Q11918: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Hawthorn Industries is a C corporation preparing tax-basis financial statements. The company has $120,000 in temporary differences that would create a $25,200 deferred tax liability The current federal income tax liability is $84,000. How should income taxes be reported on the tax-basis statements?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under the tax basis of accounting, financial statements follow IRC measurement rules and do not recognize deferred tax assets or liabilities because the concept of temporary differences arises only under GAAP (AU-C 800; ASC 740). Only the current $84,000 income tax liability is reported. Choice A is incorrect because it reflects GAAP treatment under ASC 740, which requires recognition of both current and deferred tax provisions. (See ASC 740..)$EXPL$
