-- Q11996: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$On November 15, 2025, Ridgeway Corp. purchases a 90-day U.S. Treasury bill maturing on February 13, 2026. The controller is determining whether this instrument qualifies as a cash equivalent The three-month maturity criterion is measured from which date?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$ASC 230-10-45-6 defines cash equivalents as investments with original maturities of three months or less from the date the entity purchases them. A Treasury bill with a six-month term at issuance but purchased with 60 days remaining qualifies because the holder's purchase date governs classification. Choice D is incorrect because the classification is determined at acquisition, not reassessed at each reporting date. (See ASC 230..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11996;

