-- Q12011: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Bridgewater Inc. grants 9,000 stock options on January 1, Year 1, with graded vesting: 3,000 vest after Year 1, 3,000 after Year 2, and 3,000 after Year 3. The grant-date fair value is $8 per option. Bridgewater elects the accelerated attribution method What is compensation expense in Year 1?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 718-10-35-8, the accelerated attribution method treats each vesting tranche as a separate award. Tranche 1 (3,000 × $8 over 1 year): $24,000. Tranche 2 (3,000 × $8 over 2 years): $12,000 in Year 1. Tranche 3 (3,000 × $8 over 3 years): $8,000 in Year 1. Total Year 1 = $44,000. Option B ($24,000) uses straight-line over 3 years ($72,000 ÷ 3), the alternative approach that produces lower first-year expense and higher expense in later years. (See ASC 718..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12011;

