-- Q12069: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Crestwood Software has capitalized $800,000 of development costs for an external product Cumulative amortization is $200,000, leaving unamortized cost of $600,000. Due to a competitor's product launch, estimated net realizable value drops to $450,000. What amount should Crestwood report for this asset?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 985-20-35-4, capitalized software costs for external sale are reported at the lower of unamortized cost or NRV at each balance sheet date. NRV ($450,000) is below unamortized cost ($600,000), so the asset is written down to $450,000 with a $150,000 charge to cost of sales. Choice B ignores the mandatory NRV ceiling test that distinguishes ASC 985-20 from internal-use software impairment under ASC 360. (See ASC 985-20..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12069;

