-- Q12460: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Langford Corp. issues convertible preferred stock with a beneficial conversion feature (BCF) valued at $200,000 The BCF is recognized as a discount on the preferred stock and accreted over the period to the earliest conversion date. In the issuance year, Langford accretes $80,000 of the BCF. Net income is $1,000,000 with 250,000 weighted-average common shares. How does the BCF accretion affect basic EPS?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Under ASC 260-10-45-12 and ASC 470-20-25-5, the accretion of a beneficial conversion feature on preferred stock is treated as a deemed dividend to the preferred shareholders. The $80,000 of current-year accretion is deducted from the EPS numerator, reducing income available to common shareholders to $920,000. Option A is incorrect because, although the BCF does not hit the income statement, it has a direct effect on the EPS numerator through the deemed dividend mechanism, just like declared preferred dividends. (See ASC 470-20..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12460;

