-- Q12647: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$DataCore Systems enters a change-in-control agreement with its CEO, Priya Deshmukh. Deshmukh's base amount is $500,000. Upon a qualifying change in ownership, she will receive total parachute payments of $1,800,000. A tax advisor must calculate the excise tax liability and assess the overall tax cost. What is the excise tax owed by Deshmukh, and what additional consequence applies to DataCore?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): IRC Sections 280G and 4999. Since total parachute payments ($1,800,000) equal or exceed 3x the base amount ($1,500,000), the excess parachute payment is $1,800,000 minus the base amount of $500,000 = $1,300,000. Wait — actually, excess parachute payment = total parachute payments minus base amount = $1,800,000 - $500,000 = $1,300,000. The 20% excise tax = $1,300,000 x 20% = $260,000. DataCore loses the deduction for the $1,300,000 excess under Section 280G. Let me reconsider choice A vs B. (See Section 4999.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12647;

