-- Q12904: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Caldwell purchases a 25% partnership interest for $600,000 when the partnership has a election in effect. The partnership's total inside basis is $2,000,000 (Caldwell's 25% share = $500,000). The partnership holds two asset classes: ordinary income property (basis $800,000, FMV $1,200,000) and capital gain property (basis $1,200,000, FMV $1,200,000)., how is Caldwell's $100,000 adjustment allocated?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 755, the Section 743(b) adjustment is allocated based on the difference between FMV and inside basis within each asset class. The ordinary income property class has a $400,000 built-in gain ($1,200,000 FMV - $800,000 basis), while the capital gain property has zero built-in gain. The entire $100,000 step-up is allocated to ordinary income property. Wrong (B): Capital gain property has no built-in gain, so no adjustment is allocated to it. Wrong (C): Equal allocation ignores the Section 755 requirement to allocate based on hypothetical gain analysis. Wrong (D): Proportional allocation based on total basis is not the Section 755 method; allocation follows the hypothetical sale approach. (See Section 754.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12904;

