-- Q12910: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Weston Partners has a election in effect. Partner K receives a liquidating distribution of property with an inside basis of $120,000 when Partner K's outside basis is $180,000., Partner K takes a $180,000 basis in the distributed property. Determine the adjustment to the partnership's remaining assets.$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 734(b), when a partner takes a stepped-up basis in distributed property ($180,000 vs. $120,000 inside basis), a negative adjustment of $60,000 applies to the partnership's remaining assets. The basis "gained" by the distributee must be offset by a reduction in the partnership's remaining asset basis. Wrong (A): Section 754 elections mandate adjustments for both current and liquidating distributions. Wrong (B): A positive adjustment occurs when basis is lost (partner takes lower basis), not gained. Wrong (D): The adjustment equals the difference between the partner's basis and the property's inside basis, not the original inside basis. (See Section 732.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12910;

