-- Q12933: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Oakmont Partners has NOT made a election. The partnership distributes property with an inside basis of $500,000 to Partner Z in a liquidating distribution. Partner Z's outside basis is $150,000., Partner Z takes a $150,000 basis in the property, resulting in a $350,000 basis reduction. The partnership has other assets with a total basis of $2,000,000. Evaluate whether the partnership must make a basis adjustment to its remaining assets despite lacking a election.$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 734(d), added by the American Jobs Creation Act of 2004, if a distribution results in a substantial basis reduction (the distributed property's basis exceeds the distributee's basis by more than $250,000), the partnership must make a Section 734(b) adjustment even without a Section 754 election. The $350,000 reduction exceeds the $250,000 threshold, so a mandatory negative adjustment of $350,000 applies to the remaining partnership assets. Wrong (A): Post-2004 rules require mandatory adjustments for substantial basis reductions regardless of a 754 election. Wrong (C): The adjustment is negative (step-down), not positive, because basis was "gained" by the partner at the partnership's expense. Wrong (D): The adjustment is mandatory, not voluntary, when the substantial basis reduction threshold is exceeded. (See Section 732.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12933;

