-- Q13069: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Foster completes a like-kind exchange, receiving replacement property (FMV $250,000) plus a $50,000 installment note from the buyer payable over three years. Foster's realized gain on the exchange is $120,000. How is the $50,000 note treated?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): IRC Sections 1031(b) and 453. The installment note is not like-kind property and constitutes boot. However, because boot gain recognition can be reported under the installment method, Foster may spread the $50,000 recognized gain over the three-year payment period as collections are received. Wrong (A): An installment note is not real property and does not qualify as like-kind property; it is boot. Wrong (B): The note is part of the exchange proceeds and must be included in the amount realized. Wrong (C): Boot received does not simply reduce basis; it triggers gain recognition up to the realized gain. (See Section 1031.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 13069;

