-- Q14134: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Oakridge Corp, a U.S. C corporation, has a CFC that earns $1,000,000 of GILTI tested income and pays $150,000 in foreign income taxes. Oakridge claims deemed-paid foreign tax credits (after the 80% haircut, the creditable amount is $120,000)., how must Oakridge treat the deemed-paid taxes for U.S. tax purposes?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Section 78 requires that deemed-paid foreign tax credits be included in the U.S. shareholder's gross income as a dividend. This gross-up ensures the credit offsets the additional income, maintaining parity with direct foreign tax credits. The $120,000 (after the 80% haircut) is added to Oakridge's income. Wrong (A): Deemed-paid credits are not deducted as expenses; they are claimed as credits, with the Section 78 gross-up ensuring income inclusion. Wrong (C): Section 78 explicitly requires inclusion in income; the taxes are not ignored. Wrong (D): The GILTI inclusion is not reduced by deemed-paid taxes; instead, the Section 78 gross-up increases income and the credit offsets the resulting tax. (See Section 960.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14134;

-- Q14138: Fix #9
