-- Q14139: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Grayson, a U.S. individual, owns shares in a foreign mutual fund that qualifies as a PFIC. Grayson makes a QEF election . The fund reports $30,000 of ordinary earnings and $10,000 of net capital gain for the year but distributes nothing to Grayson. What must Grayson report on his U.S. return?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 1293, a QEF election requires the U.S. shareholder to include their pro rata share of both ordinary earnings ($30,000) and net capital gain ($10,000) annually, regardless of distributions. The capital gain retains its character as long-term capital gain. Wrong (A): The QEF election specifically overrides the distribution requirement — income is included currently whether or not distributed. Wrong (B): Both ordinary earnings and net capital gain must be included annually under Section 1293(a); capital gains are not deferred. Wrong (D): Net capital gain retains its character as long-term capital gain under the QEF rules; it is not recharacterized as ordinary income. (See Section 1295.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14139;

