-- Q14265: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Northgate Industries performed its annual goodwill impairment test The carrying amount of the reporting unit (including goodwill) is $150 million. The company engaged an independent appraiser who determined the fair value of the reporting unit to be $135 million. Goodwill on the balance sheet is $40 million. The goodwill impairment loss to be recognized is:$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 350 (post-ASU 2017-04), goodwill impairment equals the excess of the reporting unit's carrying amount over its fair value, limited to the carrying amount of goodwill. Carrying amount ($150M) - Fair value ($135M) = $15M impairment, which is less than goodwill ($40M), so the impairment loss is $15M. Wrong (A): An impairment exists because the carrying amount ($150M) exceeds fair value ($135M). A zero impairment would require fair value to equal or exceed carrying amount. Wrong (C): The full goodwill amount ($40M) would only be impaired if the reporting unit's fair value were $110M or less (carrying amount minus goodwill). Wrong (D): This has no basis in the impairment calculation. The impairment is the shortfall between carrying amount and fair value. (See ASC 350..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14265;

-- Q14266: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Holloway Corp. is measuring the fair value of an investment property for its December 31, 2025, financial statements. The controller is determining the appropriate measurement date What is the measurement date under this standard?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 820, the measurement date is the specific date as of which the fair value of an asset or liability is determined. Market conditions, assumptions, and inputs are evaluated as of this date. For financial reporting, this is typically the balance sheet date. Wrong (A): The original acquisition date may be a measurement date for initial recognition, but ASC 820 applies to subsequent measurements as well. The measurement date is not fixed to the acquisition date. Wrong (B): The issuance date of financial statements is not the measurement date; fair value is measured as of the balance sheet date, which precedes issuance. Wrong (C): The date the valuation report is completed is an administrative date and may differ from the measurement date, which is the reference date for market conditions. (See ASC 820..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14266;

