-- Q14269: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Ashford Financial is measuring the fair value of its investment portfolio The controller classifies each holding within the three-level hierarchy. What are Level 1 inputs in the fair value hierarchy?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 820, Level 1 inputs are quoted prices (unadjusted) in active markets for identical assets or liabilities that the entity can access at the measurement date. These provide the most reliable evidence of fair value and require no adjustment. Wrong (A): Entity-specific assumptions describe Level 3 inputs, which are the least observable and most subjective in the hierarchy. Wrong (B): Observable inputs other than quoted prices for identical assets describe Level 2 inputs, such as quoted prices for similar assets, interest rates, and yield curves. Wrong (D): Unobservable inputs reflecting management estimates describe Level 3 inputs, the lowest level of the fair value hierarchy. (See ASC 820..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14269;

