-- Q14271: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Whitmore Consulting is allocating the purchase price of an acquired pharmaceutical company The acquirer needs to value patented drug formulations (the primary intangible asset). The analyst considers using the distributor method, which values the intangible by comparing the acquirer's full operating margins to the margins of a hypothetical distributor that sells the same products without owning the patents. The distributor method isolates the value of the patent by:$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): The distributor method compares the acquirer's actual profit margins to the margins a hypothetical distributor would earn without the subject intangible. The excess profit above the distributor's routine return is attributed to the intangible asset. This approach is used when the intangible is the primary profit driver and comparable royalty rates are unavailable. Wrong (B): Calculating reproduction cost describes the cost approach to intangible valuation, not the distributor method which is an income-based technique. Wrong (C): Applying a royalty rate describes the relief-from-royalty method, a distinct income approach that uses licensing comparables rather than distributor margin analysis. Wrong (D): Attributing all residual value to goodwill ignores the identifiable intangible. The distributor method specifically isolates the intangible's contribution before any residual is assigned to goodwill. (See ASC 805..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14271;

