-- Q14283: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$The City of Briarwood collects $420,000 in traffic fines and building code violation penalties during fiscal year 2025. Under, these fines and penalties are classified as which type of nonexchange revenue?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per GASB 33, fines and penalties are imposed nonexchange revenues because the government assesses them on nongovernmental entities without an underlying exchange transaction. They are recognized as revenue when the government has an enforceable legal claim. Wrong (A): Derived tax revenues arise from taxes on underlying exchange transactions (sales tax, income tax), not from government-imposed penalties. Wrong (C): Government-mandated transactions involve a higher-level government requiring and funding a program at a lower level. Wrong (D): Voluntary nonexchange transactions involve willing agreements between parties, not government-imposed assessments. (See GASB Statement No. 33.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14283;

-- Q14288: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$The State of Greenfield collects a per-gallon excise tax each time gasoline is purchased at retail stations. Under, this tax is classified as what type of nonexchange revenue?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per GASB 33, motor fuel taxes are derived tax revenues because they are imposed on an underlying exchange transaction — the purchase of gasoline between a buyer and seller. The government derives its revenue from taxing that exchange. Wrong (A): Imposed nonexchange revenues (property taxes, fines) are levied without an underlying exchange transaction. Wrong (B): Government-mandated transactions involve a higher-level government requiring and funding a program at a lower level. Wrong (D): Voluntary nonexchange transactions involve willing agreements between parties, not taxes on purchases. (See GASB Statement No. 33.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14288;

