-- Q14310: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Apex Global Inc. failed to maintain contemporaneous documentation for intercompany transactions with its foreign subsidiaries. The IRS determined a adjustment of $15,000,000, which constitutes a substantial valuation misstatement. What penalty applies to the underpayment attributable to this adjustment?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 6662(e), a substantial valuation misstatement triggers a 20% penalty on the underpayment. Without contemporaneous documentation under Sec. 6662(e)(3)(B), the taxpayer cannot establish reasonable cause as a defense. Wrong (A): The reasonable cause defense is unavailable when contemporaneous documentation was not maintained for transfer pricing adjustments. Wrong (B): The accuracy-related penalty for transfer pricing misstatements is 20%, not 10%. Wrong (D): The 40% penalty applies to gross valuation misstatements (400% or more of correct value), which requires a higher threshold than substantial misstatement. (See Section 482.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14310;

