-- Q14343: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$The City of Lakewood reports the following data at year-end: governmental fund balances of $8,200,000; capital assets net of depreciation of $31,400,000; general obligation bonds of $16,000,000; compensated absences of $720,000; net pension liability of $4,100,000; net OPEB liability of $2,300,000; lease liability of $950,000; deferred outflows (pensions) of $1,100,000; deferred inflows (pensions) of $600,000; deferred outflows (OPEB) of $380,000; deferred inflows (OPEB) of $210,000; unavailable property tax revenue of $460,000; and internal service fund net position of $340,000. Calculate the net position of governmental activities.$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per GASB 34, net position = fund balances ($8,200,000) + capital assets net ($31,400,000) − GO bonds ($16,000,000) − compensated absences ($720,000) − net pension liability ($4,100,000) − net OPEB liability ($2,300,000) − lease liability ($950,000) + deferred outflows pensions ($1,100,000) − deferred inflows pensions ($600,000) + deferred outflows OPEB ($380,000) − deferred inflows OPEB ($210,000) + unavailable revenue ($460,000) + ISF net position ($340,000) = $17,000,000. Wrong (A): This omits the deferred outflows and unavailable revenue adjustments. Wrong (C): This incorrectly adds the long-term liabilities instead of subtracting them. Wrong (D): This double-subtracts the pension-related deferrals. (See GASB 87.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14343;

-- Q14353: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$A county operates a municipal landfill accounted for in the general fund. During the year, the estimated landfill closure and postclosure liability increased by $850,000 The county made no cash payments toward closure costs. How does this $850,000 appear in the activity statement reconciliation?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB 18, landfill closure and postclosure costs are recognized as a long-term liability on government-wide statements as capacity is consumed. Governmental funds only record expenditures when payments are due. Since no cash payment was made, the $850,000 increase in the liability is an expense only on government-wide statements and must be subtracted in the reconciliation. Wrong (A): Adding the amount back would be incorrect; the liability increase reduces net position. Wrong (B): Landfill closure costs create a liability, not a deferred inflow of resources. Wrong (C): The treatments differ because governmental funds use modified accrual and do not recognize long-term liabilities. (See GASB 18..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14353;

-- Q14356: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$The City of Cedarville reports capital assets of $48,000,000 with accumulated depreciation of $16,500,000. Outstanding capital-related debt includes general obligation bonds of $18,000,000 (of which $2,500,000 is unspent bond proceeds held in a capital projects fund) and a lease liability of $1,400,000. Deferred amounts on refundings total $600,000 (deferred outflow). Calculate the net investment in capital assets component of net position.$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per GASB 34, paragraph 33, net investment in capital assets = capital assets net of depreciation ($48,000,000 − $16,500,000 = $31,500,000) minus capital-related debt ($18,000,000 + $1,400,000 = $19,400,000) plus unspent bond proceeds ($2,500,000) plus deferred amount on refunding ($600,000) = $31,500,000 − $19,400,000 + $2,500,000 + $600,000 = $15,200,000. Wrong (A): This is simply capital assets net of depreciation without adjusting for related debt. Wrong (B): This omits the unspent bond proceeds and deferred refunding amount. Wrong (D): This incorrectly subtracts the deferred amount on refunding instead of adding it. (See GASB 87.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14356;

