-- Q14429: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Ridgeway Corp. (U.S.) enters a 90-day forward contract to buy CHF 800,000 at a forward rate of $1.05/CHF when the spot rate is $1.03/CHF. Ridgeway designates the forward as a cash flow hedge and excludes the forward points from the effectiveness assessment How should the $16,000 forward premium be recognized?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 815-20-25, when forward points are excluded from the hedge effectiveness assessment, the initial premium (CHF 800,000 x ($1.05 - $1.03) = $16,000) is amortized to earnings on a systematic basis over the life of the hedging instrument. Wrong (A): Immediate recognition would apply only if the contract were not designated as a hedge. Wrong (C): Only the effective portion of the spot-rate change goes to OCI, not the excluded forward premium. Wrong (D): Basis adjustment applies to the hedged item's cost, not to excluded components of the derivative. (See ASC 815..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14429;

-- Q14430: Fix #9
