-- Q14444: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Marlowe Corp. (U.S.) purchases a put option on EUR 2,000,000 to hedge a forecasted euro-denominated sale. The option is designated as a cash flow hedge, and Marlowe elects to exclude time value from the effectiveness assessment At a reporting date, the option's total fair value change is a $30,000 gain, of which $22,000 relates to intrinsic value and $8,000 relates to time value. How are these components reported?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 815-20-25, when time value is excluded from the effectiveness assessment for an option, the change in intrinsic value ($22,000) is recorded in OCI as the effective hedge portion. The excluded time value component ($8,000) is recognized in earnings on a systematic and rational basis over the hedge term. Wrong (B): Recording the full $30,000 in OCI would fail to separately account for the excluded component. Wrong (C): Intrinsic value (the assessed component) goes to OCI, not earnings, while time value goes to earnings. Wrong (D): Only an undesignated derivative would have the full change in earnings; hedge designation routes the effective portion to OCI. (See ASC 815-20-25..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14444;

