-- Q14482: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Dr. Kapoor founded and serves as president of a tax-exempt educational foundation 3). She directly controls all major decisions. Dr. Kapoor sells laboratory equipment (basis $200,000, FMV $150,000) to the foundation for $150,000. Separately, the foundation owes Dr. Kapoor $80,000 in consulting fees accrued at year-end (foundation is accrual-basis, Dr. Kapoor is cash-basis), paid four months later. Evaluate the tax treatment of both transactions.$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 267(b)(9), a tax-exempt educational organization and a person who controls it are related parties. Dr. Kapoor's $50,000 loss is disallowed under Section 267(a)(1). The $80,000 consulting fee deduction is deferred under Section 267(a)(2) until Dr. Kapoor includes it in income as a cash-basis taxpayer. Wrong (B): Section 267(b)(9) expressly includes tax-exempt educational/charitable organizations and their controlling persons. Wrong (C): The consulting fee deduction is deferred, not permanently disallowed — it is allowed when Dr. Kapoor reports the income. Wrong (D): The matching rule under Section 267(a)(2) prevents the deduction until the cash-basis payee recognizes the income. (See Section 501.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14482;

