-- Q14497: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Thornton is a 25% partner in Elm Street Ventures, which allocates him a $90,000 loss for 2026. Thornton''s outside basis in the partnership is $55,000., what limits Thornton''s deduction of the allocated loss?$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14497;

-- Q14499: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Webb contributes $50,000 cash and performs $30,000 worth of accounting services in exchange for a 40% interest in Atlas Consulting LLP., the cash contribution is tax-free. However, the services component is taxable, and Webb recognizes $30,000 of ordinary income . Analyze Webb's initial outside basis in the partnership interest.$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 722, Webb's basis includes the $50,000 cash contributed. The $30,000 of services income recognized under Section 83 also creates basis, as the amount included in income becomes the basis of the interest received for services. Total basis: $50,000 + $30,000 = $80,000.
Wrong (A): This ignores the basis created by the services component. When income is recognized on the services portion, that amount adds to outside basis.
Wrong (B): This counts only the services income and ignores the $50,000 cash contribution, which creates basis under Section 722.
Wrong (C): Outside basis is not calculated as a percentage of partnership assets; it is the sum of cash plus adjusted basis of property contributed plus any income recognized. (See Section 721.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14499;

-- Q14500: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Nordic Partners has two equal partners, Ellis and Fowler. The partnership holds $200,000 of substantially appreciated inventory (basis $80,000) and $200,000 cash. Ellis receives $200,000 cash in complete liquidation of her 50% interest. Before the distribution, Ellis was entitled to 50% of the inventory (FMV $100,000, basis $40,000). Analyze the tax consequences .$EXPL$
