-- Q14501: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Brighton Corporation's S election terminates on June 30 of the current year. Shareholder Wallace has $25,000 of suspended losses from the S corporation period that were limited . Wallace's stock basis is $30,000 at the time of termination. Under the post-termination transition period (PTTP) rules of, what may Wallace do with the suspended losses?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 1366(d)(3), any suspended loss from the S corporation period may be deducted by the shareholder during the PTTP (generally one year after the termination date) to the extent of stock basis. Wallace has sufficient basis ($30,000) to absorb the $25,000 loss, reducing stock basis to $5,000.
Wrong (A): Suspended losses are not permanently disallowed; Section 1366(d)(3) specifically provides the PTTP window for deduction.
Wrong (C): Suspended S corporation losses do not convert to NOLs; they remain S corporation losses deductible only against stock basis during the PTTP.
Wrong (D): The PTTP allows deduction against any income on the shareholder's individual return, not only future S corporation income. (See Section 1377.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14501;

