-- Q14570: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$During a incorporation, the founding shareholder's only contributed asset has an adjusted basis of $50,000, and the corporation assumes a $75,000 mortgage attached to it. No other property or cash is transferred., how much gain must the shareholder recognize?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 357(c), when liabilities assumed exceed the aggregate adjusted basis of all property transferred, the excess is recognized as gain. The $75,000 liability exceeds the $50,000 basis by $25,000, which must be recognized. Wrong (A): While Section 357(a) generally excludes liabilities from boot treatment, Section 357(c) overrides this when liabilities exceed aggregate basis. Wrong (B): Only the excess of liabilities over basis triggers gain, not the entire liability amount. Wrong (D): Section 357(c) measures gain by the excess of liabilities over basis, not by reference to fair market value. (See Section 351.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14570;

