-- Q14591: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Burke transfers equipment with a basis of $45,000 and FMV of $180,000, subject to a $65,000 mortgage, to a new corporation for 100% of the stock., Burke recognizes $20,000 of gain., what is Burke's basis in the stock received?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 358, the shareholder's basis in stock received starts with the basis of property transferred ($45,000), decreased by liabilities assumed ($65,000), and increased by gain recognized ($20,000). Calculation: $45,000 − $65,000 + $20,000 = $0. The basis cannot go below zero, and this formula produces exactly zero. Wrong (A): This is the original property basis without adjusting for liabilities and recognized gain. Wrong (B): This is the amount of gain recognized, not the resulting stock basis. Wrong (C): This is the liability amount, which has no direct relationship to the resulting stock basis. (See Section 357.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14591;

