-- Q14703: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Pinehurst Retail enters a five-year operating lease on January 1, 2026, with annual payments of $120,000. For book purposes, Pinehurst records a right-of-use asset of $505,000 and a lease liability of $505,000 on the commencement date. For tax, lease payments are deductible when paid. At year-end, the ROU asset is $404,000 and the lease liability is $410,000 after the first payment and amortization. At a 21% tax rate, what net deferred tax amount is recognized?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 740, the ROU asset (book $404,000, tax $0) creates a DTL of $404,000 × 21% = $84,840. The lease liability (book $410,000, tax $0) creates a DTA of $410,000 × 21% = $86,100. The net position is a DTA of $86,100 − $84,840 = $1,260. Wrong (A): This incorrectly applies 21% to the full lease liability balance. Wrong (B): This reflects only the DTL from the ROU asset without netting the DTA from the lease liability. Wrong (D): This incorrectly applies 21% to the full initial lease amount of $505,000 ÷ 21% rather than computing separate DTAs and DTLs on each balance and netting them. (See ASC 842.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14703;

