-- Q14724: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Oakmont LLC is a private company that elected the accounting alternative for goodwill The company recognized $2,000,000 of goodwill in a business combination. Under this alternative, what is the default amortization period if the entity cannot determine a more appropriate useful life?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): ASC 350-20-35-63 provides a 10-year default amortization period on a straight-line basis when the entity elects the private company alternative and cannot determine a more appropriate useful life. This alternative allows amortization instead of the annual impairment-only model. Wrong (A): The 15-year Section 197 period applies for tax purposes, not the GAAP private company alternative. Wrong (C): Twenty years is not the default period under the alternative. Wrong (D): The private company alternative specifically permits amortization of goodwill; it is not limited to impairment test simplification. (See ASC 350-20-35-62..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14724;

