-- Q14748: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Maple Corp. acquires a business and recognizes $5,000,000 of goodwill for financial reporting purposes. The goodwill is also deductible for tax purposes over 15 years. In Year 1, tax amortization is $333,333 while book goodwill is not amortized. Assuming a 25% tax rate, what deferred tax consequence arises from the Year 1 temporary difference?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): When goodwill is deductible for tax purposes but not amortized for book purposes, the tax basis decreases below the book basis, creating a taxable temporary difference. This results in a deferred tax liability of $333,333 x 25% = $83,333 in Year 1. The initial recognition exception under ASC 740-10-25-15(d) does not apply to goodwill recognized in a business combination where book and tax goodwill exist simultaneously. Wrong (A): The temporary difference creates a DTL, not a DTA, because the tax basis is lower than the book basis. Wrong (C): The initial recognition exception does not apply when goodwill arises in a taxable business combination with simultaneous book and tax goodwill. Wrong (D): This is the full tax amortization amount, not the deferred tax effect. (See Section 197.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14748;

