-- Q14846: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$A CPA is transitioning from auditing private companies under FASB standards to auditing a municipal government under GASB standards. Apply the relevant frameworks to determine how governmental fund revenue recognition differs from commercial revenue recognition$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under modified accrual accounting (GASB Codification 1600), governmental fund revenues are recognized when measurable and available (collectible within the current period or soon enough thereafter, typically 60 days). ASC 606 uses a five-step model: identify the contract, identify performance obligations, determine transaction price, allocate to obligations, and recognize when satisfied. These are fundamentally different frameworks. Wrong (B): The frameworks use entirely different recognition criteria — availability versus performance obligation satisfaction. Wrong (C): This reverses which framework applies to which entity type. Wrong (D): Governmental funds use modified accrual, not cash basis — revenues can be recognized before cash receipt if they are available. (See ASC 606..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14846;

