-- Q14875: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Apex Industries acquires 100% of Beacon Corp. in a business combination. Beacon sponsors a defined benefit pension plan with a PBO of $8,000,000, plan assets at fair value of $6,500,000, and $900,000 of unrecognized prior service cost and $400,000 of unrecognized net actuarial loss in Beacon's AOCI. Evaluate how Apex should account for Beacon's pension plan in the acquisition-date balance sheet and$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 805-20-25 and ASC 715-30-35-79, the acquirer recognizes the acquired pension plan at its funded status on the acquisition date (PBO $8,000,000 minus plan assets $6,500,000 = $1,500,000 net liability). The acquiree's AOCI balances for prior service cost and actuarial losses are eliminated in the business combination and do not carry forward.
Wrong (B): Adding AOCI balances to the funded status would double-count items already reflected in the PBO measurement, overstating the liability.
Wrong (C): AOCI balances of the acquiree are eliminated in a business combination; they do not transfer to the acquirer's consolidated equity.
Wrong (D): ASC 715 requires measurement using the PBO (which includes future salary assumptions), not the ABO, for balance sheet recognition of funded status. (See ASC 715..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14875;

