-- Q15064: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$A defined benefit pension plan prepares its own financial statements The plan holds equity securities at fair value of $45,000,000, bonds at fair value of $30,000,000, and has an actuarially determined present value of accumulated plan benefits of $68,000,000. The plan paid $4,200,000 in benefits during the year. What financial statements and key disclosures does require the plan to present?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): ASC 960-205-45 requires a defined benefit plan to present a statement of net assets available for benefits and a statement of changes in net assets available for benefits. ASC 960-20-50 requires the actuarial present value of accumulated plan benefits to be presented either in a separate financial statement or disclosed in the notes. Wrong (B): Pension plans do not follow corporate entity financial statement formats; they use plan-specific statements. Wrong (C): A statement of cash flows is not the primary required statement; ASC 960 focuses on net assets and accumulated plan benefits. Wrong (D): Actuarial information about accumulated plan benefits is a required element, not optional. (See ASC 960..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 15064;

