-- Q15073: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Ridgeline Corp. settles a portion of its defined benefit obligation by purchasing annuity contracts from Pacific Life Insurance Co. for $1,850,000. The settled portion of the PBO is $1,720,000. Ridgeline has unrecognized prior service cost of $300,000 and an unrecognized net loss of $180,000 in AOCI. The total PBO before settlement is $5,200,000. Evaluate the proper accounting for this settlement$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 715-30-35-79, a settlement requires recognizing a pro rata portion of the unrecognized prior service cost and net gain or loss from AOCI in earnings, based on the percentage of the PBO settled ($1,720,000 / $5,200,000 = 33.1%), plus the difference between the settlement price and the settled PBO. Wrong (A): Omits the required proportional recognition of AOCI items. Wrong (C): Confuses the cash payment with pension expense, ignoring the existing PBO offset. Wrong (D): Settlements require immediate recognition in earnings, not deferral to AOCI. (See ASC 715..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 15073;

