-- Q15121: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Timberline Manufacturing carries inventory at $2,000,000 and records a $400,000 write-down to net realizable value Before the write-down, the current ratio was 2.00 and inventory turnover was 5.0. Which statement about the immediate ratio effects is correct?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per ASC 330-10-35, the write-down reduces inventory (a current asset) by $400,000, lowering the current ratio numerator while the denominator (current liabilities) stays the same, so the current ratio falls. Inventory turnover (COGS / average inventory) increases because the denominator shrinks with the lower inventory balance. Wrong (A): Inventory turnover increases, not decreases, because the inventory denominator is smaller. Wrong (C): The current ratio decreases because current assets fall with the write-down. Wrong (D): Reverses both effects — the current ratio falls and inventory turnover rises. (See ASC 330-10-35..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 15121;

