  stem = $EXPL$After the December 31, 2025 balance sheet date but before its financial statements are issued, Calloway Enterprises experiences several significant events. The CFO must evaluate each event What are the two types of subsequent events defined by this standard?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per ASC 855-10-25, the two types are recognized subsequent events (Type I), which provide additional evidence about conditions existing at the balance sheet date and require adjustment, and nonrecognized subsequent events (Type II), which provide evidence about conditions arising after the balance sheet date and require disclosure only. Wrong (A): Materiality is a separate concept that applies to both types. Wrong (C): Probable and possible are contingency classifications under ASC 450, not subsequent event types. Wrong (D): Both types may require disclosure; this is not how they are categorized. (See ASC 855..)$EXPL$
