-- Q15654: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Lakewood Partners acquires a 30% interest in a privately held biotech startup, Helix Genomics, for $6,500,000. Helix has volatile earnings, limited financial history, and no readily determinable fair value for its equity. Lakewood's investment committee is deciding between applying the equity method and electing the fair value option Evaluate which approach best reflects economic reality given these circumstances.$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 825-10-25, the fair value option is available but requires reliable fair value measurement. For a private entity with volatile earnings and no readily determinable fair value, estimating fair value each period introduces significant measurement uncertainty. The equity method under ASC 323 provides a more reliable representation by tracking the investor's share of investee earnings. Wrong (A): Reducing complexity alone does not justify the fair value option when measurement reliability is questionable. Wrong (B): The equity method is not categorically superior — fair value can be more relevant when reliable measurements exist. Wrong (C): While the irrevocability statement is true under ASC 825-10-25-4, this alone does not determine which approach best reflects economic reality. (See ASC 825..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 15654;

