-- Q15667: Fix #9
UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$On September 1, 2026, Whitfield Corp. purchases 5,000 shares of a publicly traded company for $42 per share, classified as an equity investment At December 31, 2026, the shares trade at $38 per share. What amount should Whitfield recognize as an unrealized loss for the year ended December 31, 2026?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 321-10-35-1, equity securities with readily determinable fair values are measured at fair value with changes recognized in net income. The unrealized loss is (5,000 × $42) − (5,000 × $38) = $210,000 − $190,000 = $20,000, recognized in earnings. Wrong (B): Equity securities under ASC 321 do not use OCI — all fair value changes go through net income. Wrong (C): There is no temporary-decline exception for equity securities under ASC 321; all changes are recognized each period. Wrong (D): $42,000 does not correspond to any valid calculation in this scenario. (See ASC 321..)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 15667;

